---
description: Apply Flow workflow and document conventions when planning work, invoking skills, or creating and changing documentation.
alwaysApply: true
---

Flow workflow authority: `FLOW.md`.

Before producing an artifact or following a skill that writes files, read the relevant sections of `FLOW.md`.

Use third-party skills for specialized methodology. Flow controls canonical document ownership, paths, naming conventions, and documentation lifecycle.

For product scope, consult `PRODUCT.md`. For UI or interaction, consult `DESIGN.md`. For technical boundaries, consult `ARCHITECTURE.md`. For project-specific terminology, consult `GLOSSARY.md`. Read only the context relevant to the task.

Do not duplicate documentation or create documents that the task does not need. Existing decisions require authorization before reversal.
